---
import Education from '../../layouts/Education.astro';
import TeachingDownloads from '../../components/TeachingDownloads.astro';
import {url} from '../../lib/site';
const paths=[
  ['One class or workshop','Teach a 50-minute lesson','A complete fictional case, student worksheet, timed agenda and worked answers. Begin with an educator or authorized host.','/learn/teach/'],
  ['A university course','Develop a faculty-owned seminar','An eight-meeting outline maps the ten-chapter textbook. Start with a willing instructor and the institution’s own curriculum process.','/learn/universities/'],
  ['A student-led group','Run a first meeting','Four beginner meetings, rotating roles, a draft constitution and a handover plan. Students check their own campus rules.','/learn/clubs/'],
  ['School enrichment','Adapt with an adult educator','A proposed ages 14–18 version uses paper and fictional examples. Teachers choose the fit, supervision and approval route.','/learn/schools/'],
];
---
<Education title="Put generosity on the syllabus." description="Ready-to-adapt lessons, a sample seminar and club materials for studying charity as a system." filePath="src/pages/learn/index.astro">
  <a slot="actions" class="btn" href={url('/learn/teach/')}>Try the 50-minute lesson</a><a slot="actions" class="btn btn-ghost" href="#materials">Get the teaching pack</a>
  <section><p class="eyebrow">Choose a starting point</p><div class="education-grid">{paths.map(([label,title,text,path])=><article class="education-card"><p class="eyebrow">{label}</p><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p><a href={url(path)}>Explore this route →</a></article>)}</div></section>
  <section><h2>Study the system. Question the framework.</h2><p>Follow generosity through givers, signals, channels, work and outcomes. Ask what changed, what would have happened otherwise and whose voice can change the next decision. Describe relief, repair, prevention, structure and source without grading people or charities.</p><p>Charitology offers a particular systems lens within an existing field of philanthropy education. The <a href={url('/learn/universities/#existing-models')}>university guide links existing teaching models</a> to learn from. Our own framework and teaching proposals remain open to challenge.</p><div class="education-callout"><p><strong>Teaching drafts, not an adopted curriculum.</strong> These activities and timings have not been piloted. We claim no institutional approval, academic credit, recognized chapters or measured learning benefits. An instructor can adapt and critique the material without endorsing Charitology.</p></div></section>
  <section id="materials"><p class="eyebrow">Use and adapt</p><h2>Take an editable pack.</h2><p>The Markdown files open in a text editor and can be copied into your institution’s teaching system. The complete pack includes facilitator answers. Charitology’s authored materials are <a href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology/blob/main/CONTENT-LICENSE.md">CC BY 4.0</a>: credit Charitology, link the source and identify changes. Cited third-party material keeps its own rights.</p><TeachingDownloads ids={['complete-pack','start-here','facilitator-guide','student-worksheet','university-syllabus','club-starter','school-pack']} /><p class="education-small">Version 0.1 · All cases and numerical results in the activity are invented. No donation, account, public post or disclosure of personal beliefs or finances is required.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Keep learning or organize the work.</h2><div class="education-grid"><article class="education-card"><h3>Continue independently</h3><p>The existing <a href={url('/programs/principles-course/')}>ten-unit self-study course</a> has readings, explained questions and practice. Its completion record is nonaccredited. The <a href={url('/record/principles/read/')}>complete textbook</a> remains available to read and print.</p></article><article class="education-card"><h3>Coordinate a teaching pilot</h3><p>Adult organizers can manually use <a href="https://os.charitology.org/#module/projects">Charity OS Projects and tasks</a> and <a href="https://os.charitology.org/#module/resources">Resources</a> for a fictional planning example. These links open existing modules after sign-in and organization choice; they create no record. The teaching activity works fully on paper and asks for no learner accounts or records.</p></article></div></section>
</Education>
